1	/**
2	 * DockerRunAdapter — ExecutorPort adapter for the local-docker profile (T8).
3	 *
4	 * submit() registers the handle with the broker, then runs:
5	 *   docker run -d \
6	 *     --name exec-<handle> \
7	 *     --network agents-net \
8	 *     --entrypoint /platform/runner.js \
9	 *     --restart=no \
10	 *     -v /platform-bin:/platform:ro \
11	 *     -v /workspaces/<task>:/workspace:rw \
12	 *     -e RESULT_PATH ... -e CALLBACK_URL ... \
13	 *     --label platform.handle=<handle> \
14	 *     executor:current
15	 *
16	 * The container runs the runner wrapper as PID 1. When the wrapper exits
17	 * (after POSTing result to broker), the container exits naturally.
18	 * `--rm` is NOT used so docker logs / inspect remain available until ack().
19	 *
20	 * Wrapper-crash safety net:
21	 *   `docker wait <container_id>` is run in background. If the container
22	 *   exits without a corresponding broker callback arriving within crashGraceMs,
23	 *   the adapter synthesises a "failed" completion via the broker's callback URL.
24	 *
25	 * ack():
26	 *   Runs `docker rm <container_id>` to clean up the exited container, and
27	 *   unlinks the result file. Delegates to broker.ack() to commit consumption.
28	 *
29	 * Orphan sweep:
30	 *   A periodic sweep scans `docker ps -a -f label=platform.handle=<handle>`
31	 *   for exited containers whose handles are no longer in the supervision map
32	 *   (i.e. have already been acked or are unknown) and removes them.
33	 */
